          "where": "Mission Design",
          "quote": "Earth radius of 6371km plus a proposed altitude of 600km as previously explained."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "Major design segments are addressed using STK and literature. However, multiple technical errors occur: Kourou is stated as 45.05°N instead of ~5.2°N; the 600 km SSO inclination is mistakenly recorded as prograde 87.79° instead of 97.79°; semi-major axis calculation has an addition error (6371+600=7171 km); and a 580 s mean access duration is misreported as nearly twenty minutes."
    },
